WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:01.430
- Is it kind of an amazing thing,

00:00:01.430 --> 00:00:03.060
I know you've probably been
asked this a million times,

00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:06.740
but to be a part of
something so monumental,

00:00:06.740 --> 00:00:08.370
like, so important in pop culture?

00:00:08.370 --> 00:00:10.300
Like, everyone rushed home Thursday nights

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:11.440
to watch that show, like, we,

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:13.590
literally, everyone I know watched it.

00:00:13.590 --> 00:00:15.123
Like, that's incredible.
- Yeah, it's funny now.

00:00:15.123 --> 00:00:16.620
I mean, it felt really huge,

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:18.940
but the way things are now with, like,

00:00:18.940 --> 00:00:20.630
social media, and streaming,

00:00:20.630 --> 00:00:23.000
and your ability to binge watch something.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:27.130
That was back before, you
know, they got VRCs back then.

00:00:27.130 --> 00:00:28.139
Nobody knew how to

00:00:28.139 --> 00:00:29.080
set the thing--
- You had to wait.

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:31.310
- Yeah, but nobody could
figure out how to tape a show.

00:00:31.310 --> 00:00:32.560
- I did.
- If you were right there,

00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:33.500
you could press record, (laughing)

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:36.613
but, like, to program
it, you got the news.

00:00:36.613 --> 00:00:37.890
You know what I mean?

00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:42.730
So, but now, it feels
somehow just as relevant now

00:00:42.730 --> 00:00:45.370
as it did back then.
- Yeah!

00:00:45.370 --> 00:00:47.220
- It's funny 'cause we're
all so much older now.

00:00:47.220 --> 00:00:48.053
You know what I mean?

00:00:48.053 --> 00:00:50.790
And it's on TV, you think, "God
look at, they're so young!",

00:00:50.790 --> 00:00:51.623
and then you come on

00:00:51.623 --> 00:00:55.530
and you're like, "Jesus!" (laughing)

00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:57.351
- I feel like that with my career as well.

00:00:57.351 --> 00:00:59.300
Could you leave the house though,

00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:01.330
back in the height of it all?

00:01:01.330 --> 00:01:02.830
'Cause I remember we were actually

00:01:02.830 --> 00:01:04.160
both at the same award show.

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:05.550
I can't remember what it was.

00:01:05.550 --> 00:01:06.660
But it was during "American Idol",

00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:08.890
and y'all, or a couple
of y'all were there,

00:01:08.890 --> 00:01:11.400
and everybody was swarming around y'all,

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:14.020
and so I was like, "Oh my
God, that's gotta be rough".

00:01:14.020 --> 00:01:15.810
- Yeah, well you know,
there's some weird things

00:01:15.810 --> 00:01:18.623
that happened, you know, back then.

00:01:18.623 --> 00:01:20.614
- Like what?
- I remember one time,

00:01:20.614 --> 00:01:23.370
(laughing) so it was
during the week, it was

00:01:23.370 --> 00:01:25.470
just like during the afternoon
and I happened to be flipping

00:01:25.470 --> 00:01:28.720
channels, I was watching the
news, and for some reason

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:32.650
they had like a split screen
on the TV, six quadrants,

00:01:32.650 --> 00:01:33.750
well it wouldn't be quadrants,

00:01:33.750 --> 00:01:37.350
but six equal...
- (laughing) Six four.

00:01:37.350 --> 00:01:41.660
- And each was a live shot
of each one of our houses,

00:01:41.660 --> 00:01:43.407
like a helicopter shot.

00:01:43.407 --> 00:01:44.657
"They have the cast of "Friends" houses!",

00:01:44.657 --> 00:01:47.727
and I was like, "Okay, what is this,

00:01:47.727 --> 00:01:49.247
"what's going on here?",
and I'm watching it,

00:01:49.247 --> 00:01:52.030
and it was like a, not,
there was no information,

00:01:52.030 --> 00:01:54.540
and no news really,
just showing the houses.

00:01:54.540 --> 00:01:57.977
And I remember looking close
at my house and thinking,

00:01:57.977 --> 00:02:01.360
"I need a new roof". (laughing)

00:02:01.360 --> 00:02:03.810
So the helicopter flies
away, I get the ladder out,

00:02:03.810 --> 00:02:06.583
and I go up there, and I'm like, "Shoot!".

